 text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "up to one's ears ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having more than you can manage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not going to be up to my ears in paper I don't need.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about learning and the Internet.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to input ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm inputting every old sheet I have in there, starting tomorrow! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "naive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "innocently unaware ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Of course I was a little naive.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to plug into", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be connected to, or know what is going on", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are always going to be plugged into the magic screen whether you want them to be or not. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "perk", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advantage or benefit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The digital world has its perks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "streamlined", "type": "name"}, {"content": "simpler and more effective", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The application process is more streamlined. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "information highway", "type": "name"}, {"content": "digital communication system ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The world of education travels the information highway these days. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About the Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use different tenses in the future to express different events or situations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong italic\">Be going to</span> describes intentions or plans. At the moment of speaking the plans have already been made. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Finally someone is going to keep all of my files for me! I'm not going to be up to my ears in paper I don't need.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Present Continuous</span> describes fixed arrangements, especially social and travel arrangements. A time reference is usually included.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I'm inputting every old sheet I have in there, starting tomorrow!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> describes an event which will be happening at a future point. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Some students will be participating in distance and online learning courses.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Students are going to find there is improved access to school and course information. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Students are choosing their courses in the summer, long before they arrive on campus in the fall.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will be moving into the paperless future!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "If vs. Whether in the Unreal Conditional ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Unreal Conditional to talk about hypothetical situations and events, or outcomes that are unlikely to be true.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> with the Unreal Conditional to say that the possible outcomes of a hypothetical condition have been thought about, or to suggest that you are unsure about something. They are usually interchangeable.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Do you know <span class=\"strong\">whether</span>/<span class=\"strong\">if</span> the people in your extended family had access to a computer when they were young?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Whether</span> can be followed immediately by <span class=\"italic\">or not</span>. <br/>When you use <span class=\"italic\">if, ... or not</span>, the <span class=\"italic\">or not</span> is at the end of the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I don't know <span class=\"strong\">whether or not</span> you have considered the impact of the Internet on learning. <br/>I don't know <span class=\"strong\">if</span> you have considered the impact of the Internet <span class=\"strong\">or not</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I don't know whether or not you have considered how learning has changed in the digital age. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Many people still didn't know whether this new technology would even survive to 2001.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They are always going to be plugged into the magic screen whether you want them to be or not. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Does it matter if these courses are at home or abroad?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Assignments and feedback are given out over the net whether you take a course online or in classrooms.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Divide a paper in half and write down both the positive and not so positive aspects of taking a course in a traditional classroom setting or taking a course online. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Come up with 5 or 6 ideas for each type of course.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write up a short presentation as if you were considering taking the same course online or in a classroom in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your ideas to a partner or group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Open a discussion on what you have presented.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I come up with 5 or 6 ideas on the positive and not so positive aspects of taking a course online or in a classroom. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I prepare a short presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use future tenses in my presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use 'if' and/or 'whether' in my presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I open a discussion on my ideas.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le16ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "type": "sena"}